# The command palette: everything the app can do, found by name.
#
# What this holds down is the shape of the list — that an empty box is not a wall of commands,
# that the best match is first, that a command which cannot run is still found with its reason —
# and that choosing a row really runs it. The rules themselves are PaletteRulesTests'; this is
# the palette in the window, on real data.

tree .
refresh

# --- Nothing typed: pins, recents, suggestions, then the categories ---

palette
assert-palette-open
shot 01-empty
assert-palette-row # Suggested
assert-palette-row # All commands
assert-palette-row tabs:
assert-palette-row view:
# Not the catalogue: the box is empty, so nothing is listed that was not asked for or earned.
assert-no-palette-row Close other tabs
assert-no-palette-row Reverse sort order
# With nothing selected the suggestions are about getting somewhere.
assert-palette-row Edit address
assert-no-palette-row Rename

# --- Typing: the best match first, and found by other words for it ---

palette type new
shot 02-typed-new
assert-palette-order New tab | New folder
palette type branch
assert-palette-selected Toggle flat view
palette type ctrl+b
assert-palette-selected Toggle flat view
palette type treemap
assert-palette-selected Analyse disk usage
palette type dupl
assert-palette-row Find duplicates

# A command that cannot run is still found, dimmed, with the reason — rather than seeming not to exist.
palette type rename
assert-palette-selected Rename
assert-palette-hint Nothing is selected
shot 03-unavailable
palette pick
assert-palette-open
palette close
assert-palette-closed

# --- Choosing runs it, and it is remembered for this session only ---

palette
palette type new tab
palette pick
assert-palette-closed
assert-tabs 2

palette
assert-palette-order # Recent | New tab
palette close

# With something selected, the suggestions are the things done to a selection.
select notes.txt
palette
assert-palette-row Rename
assert-palette-row Copy as path
assert-no-palette-row Edit address
shot 04-with-selection
palette close
deselect

# --- Pins ---

palette
palette type toggle flat
palette pin
palette clear
assert-palette-order # Pinned | Toggle flat view
shot 05-pinned
palette pick
assert-flat
palette
palette type toggle flat
palette pin
palette clear
assert-no-palette-row # Pinned
palette close
flat off

# --- A category narrows; choosing its row types its token ---

palette
palette type view:
shot 06-category
assert-palette-row Toggle hidden items
assert-palette-row Sort by size
assert-no-palette-row Close tab
palette type view: sort
assert-palette-order Sort by name | Sort by size
assert-no-palette-row Toggle hidden items
palette type book:
palette close

# --- Named things ---

save-workspace Projects
palette
palette type projects
assert-palette-selected Projects
palette type keyboard
assert-palette-row Keyboard
palette type dark
assert-palette-row Dark
palette close

# --- A path is a destination ---

palette open Docu
assert-no-palette-row # Go to
palette close

go Documents
run nav.goto
assert-palette-open
assert-palette-row # Go to
assert-palette-row Archive
shot 07-goto
palette down 3
palette pick
assert-palette-closed
assert-path Archive

# --- On the settings page only what works there can run ---

settings general
palette
shot 08-over-settings
palette type new tab
assert-palette-hint Not while Settings is open
palette type keyboard shortcuts
palette pick
assert-palette-closed
settings close

# --- The chord that opens it is live everywhere, and closes it too ---

assert-key Ctrl+Shift+P list app.palette
assert-key Ctrl+Shift+P text app.palette
assert-key F1 other app.palette
key Ctrl+Shift+P
assert-palette-open
assert-key Ctrl+T text none
key Ctrl+Shift+P
assert-palette-closed

assert-not-launched
